
.TH Oxcaml_functor_alias 3 "" "Odoc" "OCaml Library"
.SH Name
Oxcaml_functor_alias
.SH Synopsis
.sp 
.in 2
\fBModule Oxcaml_functor_alias\fR
.in 
.sp 
.fi 
A functor whose result aliases its argument, applied by include functor\.
.nf 
.sp 
.fi 
OxCaml 5\.4 rejects such an alias, as OCaml does, so this is kept apart from the oxcaml\.mli case and runs on earlier versions of OxCaml only\.
.nf 
.SH Documentation
.sp 
.nf 
\f[CB]module\fR Make (T : \f[CB]sig\fR \.\.\. \f[CB]end\fR) : \f[CB]sig\fR \.\.\. \f[CB]end\fR
.sp 
\f[CB]type\fR t
.sp 
\f[CB]type\fR 'a p
.sp 
\f[CB]module\fR X : \f[CB]sig\fR \.\.\. \f[CB]end\fR
.sp 
\f[CB]module\fR \f[CB]type\fR S = \f[CB]sig\fR
.br 
.ti +2
\f[CB]type\fR u
.br 
\f[CB]end\fR
.sp 
\f[CB]val\fR via_module_type_include : unit
.sp 
\f[CB]module\fR Aliased : \f[CB]sig\fR \.\.\. \f[CB]end\fR
.fi 
.br 
.ti +2
The input module itself\. It should contain everything from the top level module
.nf 

